✅ 12. Difference Between wait() and sleep()

12.1 Definition

wait()
🔴 wait() is a method of the Object class.
🔴 It is used for inter-thread communication.

It causes the current thread to:
🔴 Release the monitor lock.
🔴 Enter the WAITING (or TIMED_WAITING for timed wait) state.
🔴 Wait until another thread notifies it or it is interrupted.

sleep()
🔴 sleep() is a static method of the Thread class.
🔴 It is used to pause the current thread for a specified amount of time.
🔴 It does not release the monitor lock.
🔴 After the timeout expires, the thread becomes RUNNABLE.

12.2 Why Do We Need Them?

🔴 wait() : Used when one thread depends on another.
Example:

Producer
↓
Produces Data
↓
notify()
↓
Consumer Continues

🔴 sleep() : Used when a thread simply wants to pause.

Example:

Retry API
↓
Sleep 3 Seconds
↓
Retry Again

12.3 Example of wait()
Object lock = new Object();

synchronized (lock) {
    lock.wait();
}

12.4 Example of sleep()
Thread.sleep(5000);

12.5 Internal Working
🔴 wait()

Acquire Lock
↓
wait()
↓
Release Lock
↓
WAITING
↓
notify()
↓
RUNNABLE
↓
Acquire Lock Again
↓
Continue

🔴 sleep()

Running
↓
sleep()
↓
TIMED_WAITING
↓
Time Over
↓
RUNNABLE
↓
Continue

Notice:
No lock is released.

12.6 Biggest Difference
🔴 wait()

Acquire Lock
↓
wait()
↓
Release Lock ✅

🔴 sleep()

Acquire Lock
↓
sleep()
↓
Keep Lock ❌
This is the most important interview point.

12.7 Example Showing the Difference
🔴 wait()
synchronized (lock) {
    lock.wait();
}

What happens?

Thread
↓
Releases Lock
↓
WAITING

Now another thread can enter the synchronized block.

sleep()
synchronized (lock) {
    Thread.sleep(5000);
}

Current thread: TIMED_WAITING

But

Still owns lock
Other threads remain

BLOCKED

12.8 Complete Comparison Table

| Feature                       | `wait()`                             | `sleep()`          |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------ |
| Class                         | `Object`                             | `Thread`           |
| Static                        | ❌ No                                | ✅ Yes             |
| Releases Lock                 | ✅ Yes                               | ❌ No              |
| Requires synchronized         | ✅ Yes                               | ❌ No              |
| Purpose                       | Thread Communication                 | Delay Execution    |
| State                         | `WAITING` / `TIMED_WAITING`          | `TIMED_WAITING`    |
| Wakes Up                      | `notify()`, `notifyAll()`, interrupt | Timeout, interrupt |
| Throws `InterruptedException` | ✅ Yes                               | ✅ Yes             |
| Used In                       | Producer-Consumer                    | Retry, Delay       |



